<title>USA: Clothing tops NY district import list for 1996.</title>
<headline>Clothing tops NY district import list for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 643,861 tonnes of commodities (excluding mail) were imported through the New York Customs district in 1996, the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said.</p>
<p>The top ten unloaded commodities in tonnes and as percentage of total New York district air imports and the 1995 tonnages are:</p>
<p> Commodity		   1996	As pct of   1995</p>
<p>					    '96 total</p>
<p> 1. Woven apparel	  103,533     16.1    101,312</p>
<p> 2. Machinery		 72,934     11.3     73,372</p>
<p> 3. Knit Apparel	    61,858	9.6     61,805</p>
<p> 4. Electrical Machinery  46,978	7.3     47,895</p>
<p> 5. Vegetables		36,550	5.7     29,428</p>
<p> 6. Footwear		  27,385	4.3     33,187</p>
<p> 7. Optical Med. Inst.    26,949	4.2     25,649</p>
<p> 8. Book, Newspaper	 18,621	2.9     18,458</p>
<p> 9. Leather, Saddollary   16,725	2.6     16,330</p>
<p> 10. Plastic		  15,960	2.5     15,217</p>
<p>Total NY district	  643,861		 637,827</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
